: null}, {"t_ms": 53062, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NoqpchAj2RFsRAosHE6v4v", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53062, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NoqpchAj2RFsRAosHE6v4v", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54390, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Q215g28i4vUi8o93zMTemZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54690, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Q215g28i4vUi8o93zMTemZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54690, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q215g28i4vUi8o93zMTemZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58851, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The latest one, v2.3.1, was failing with an 18% error rate, and the release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n   - My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time.\n   - A second attempt finished the rollback in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west).\n   - checkout-api now reports healthy, and its error rate is down to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** The incident creation request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate and no second page. The incident covers the failure, the rollback and the partial-rollout problem. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013q1K49v1GNs1HC4iadk551", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jg2XJscjq2ugZneKNVpMU1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CkLRo5z5EAVGhXZvX3JQe2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K7k2t6ztk9bok3bo7xjTb7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Partial rollback: us-east is on v2.3.0, but the other regions are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WxJnjBwBLFijf9Tremx5jk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VUMSqpmjF57YmgGvJpksP2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WJzuRsQuXCGyfzKeFaRBn8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NoqpchAj2RFsRAosHE6v4v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. It was rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so it was skipped. The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions for a short time. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 everywhere, reports healthy, and has an error rate of 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error during the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Q215g28i4vUi8o93zMTemZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open, and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The latest one, v2.3.1, was failing with an 18% error rate, and the release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n   - My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time.\n   - A second attempt finished the rollback in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west).\n   - checkout-api now reports healthy, and its error rate is down to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** The incident creation request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate and no second page. The incident covers the failure, the rollback and the partial-rollout problem. It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}